  path="/about/okubo/"
>
  <section class="dojo-list">
    <div class="page-container">

      <div class="section__title-area">
        <span class="section-label">PROFILE</span>
        <h1 class="section-title">Katsumi Okubo</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="profile-detail">

        <p class="profile-detail__role">
          Chairman, All Japan Seishinkai Karate Federation<br />
          Founder of ISKF · Soke of Seishinryu Kenpo Karate-do
        </p>

        <h2 class="detail-page__heading">Profile</h2>

        <div class="detail-page__img-text-pair">

          <div class="detail-media--med">
            <figure>
              <img
                src="/assets/images/about/okubo/img_okubo_fv.jpg"
                alt="Katsumi Okubo"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </figure>
          </div>

          <div class="profile-detail__body">

            <p>
              Began studying karate in 1972. He trained with the karate club
              at Kotoni Technical High School and later studied Okinawan
              traditional martial arts at Tokai University, where he served
              as captain of the club in 1979.<br />

              In 1977, he was appointed by Soke Kikuchi as the youngest
              Seishinryu branch chief, taking charge of the Sapporo Branch.<br />

              In addition to karate, he studied Aikido during university.
              During his service in the Japan Ground Self-Defense Force,
              he also studied Jukendo (bayonet fighting), unarmed combat,
              and Jujutsu. He was awarded 3rd Dan by the Soke.<br />

              During his military service, he established the Seishinryu
              Engaru Branch and Rumoi Branch.
            </p>

            <p>
              Following the death of his Soke, he reorganized the Sapporo
              Branch in 1986 and established the permanent training facility
              "Seishinkan Okubo Dojo."<br />

              Initially, he joined the Japan Seishinryu Karate-do Federation,
              headed by the former deputy head of the main dojo. He later
              left the organization and joined the Seishinryu Karate-do
              Association, an umbrella organization for Seishinryu groups,
              and continued his activities centered in Sapporo.<br />

              In 2004, the organization developed from a private local dojo
              into the Non-Profit Organization All Japan Seishinkai, which
              received certification from Hokkaido and was registered with
              the Legal Affairs Bureau.<br />

              As the number of branches grew, he established the All Japan
              Seishinkai Karate Federation. In 2011, following the establishment
              of its first overseas branch in Sri Lanka, he founded the
              international organization International Seishinryu Karate-do
              Federation (ISKF).<br />

              In 2012, he was awarded 10th Dan and the title of Soke
              (second-generation successor) by the association, becoming
              a completely independent organization.
            </p>

            <p>
              He holds 8th Dan recognized by the National Protective
              Equipment Karate Federation, 8th Dan recognized by the
              Toko Association, and 10th Dan recognized by WUKO
              (World Union of Karate Organizations). He also holds the
              Japanese Chief Instructor qualification from FIKM and has
              received honorary 10th Dan from Seishito-ryu Sanshinkan
              International and the World Kobayashi-ryu Karate Kobudo
              Association (USA).<br />

              He later incorporated techniques and philosophies from the
              various styles he studied through his own training and named
              his school's style "Seishinryu Kenpo Karate-do."<br />

              Today, he serves as the Soke and Chairman of ISKF, which has
              more than 4,000 members across approximately 150 dojos in
              Japan and overseas.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="detail-page__img-text-pair--reverse">

          <div class="detail-media--med">
            <figure>
              <img
                src="/assets/images/about/okubo/img_okubo_22.jpg"
                alt="Katsumi Okubo"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </figure>
          </div>

          <div>

            <h2 class="detail-page__heading">Career History</h2>

            <div class="profile-detail__body">
              <p>
                Served at the Japan Ground Self-Defense Force bases in
                Engaru and Rumoi. After returning home, he joined
                Suzuki Jihan Hokkaido Co., Ltd., where he worked in sales,
                later serving as manager of the Ebetsu Sales Office and
                the company's East Sales Office. He eventually became
                head of the Sales Planning Group at the head office,
                where he was responsible for the company's transition
                to IT as well as events and advertising.<br />

                After retiring, he served as a director of the Toko
                Association Foundation. He currently operates a martial
                arts equipment store, Toyo Budo-gu, alongside his karate
                activities.
              </p>
            </div>

            <h2 class="detail-page__heading">Organizations and Affiliations</h2>

            <div class="profile-detail__body">
              <p>
                <a
                  href="https://urkf-uechiryu.com/avales/"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener"
                >
                  Advisor, World Uechi-ryu Karate-do Federation
                </a>,
                Chairman of IKMA, Honorary Member of Seishito-ryu
                Sanshinkan, and others.<br />

                He has also served as Advisor to the National Protective
                Equipment Karate Federation, Advisor to the Okinawa
                Kobayashi-ryu Karate Kobudo Federation, Director of the
                Hokkaido Mainichi Cultural Association, and
                <a
                  href="http://thewrbbof.com/holiday.html"
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener"
                >
                  Director of WRBBOF
                </a>.<br />

                He has also served as the East Asia Regional Representative
                of WUKO-ad and Advisor to the Pan American Karate Federation.
              </p>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

